{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe edit-then-re-review loop is common and hazardous as two shell commands, and claim's recovery text (src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:213-215) tells the user to run review-plan then claim by hand. Operator approved both flags. OSS precedent favors embedding prerequisite verification in the consuming verb (cargo publish verifies by default; terraform apply consumes a staleness-checked plan artifact) over new fused commands.\n\n## Approach\n(1) `rebar edit <id> ... --review`: edit_cli's hand-rolled parser (src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:528-561) treats every --name as requiring a value, so `--review` is handled as an explicit valueless flag checked BEFORE the field loop (popped from argv, the same way a boolean flag must bypass the --key=value pathway); after edit_core commits the EDIT event, invoke rebar.llm.review_plan(ticket_id, sign=True) and map the returned verdict dict to the process exit status via _cli._llm_commands._disposition_exit_code(result, indeterminate_code=2) — the same mapping the review-plan CLI applies (0 PASS / 1 BLOCK / 2 INDETERMINATE / 11 retryable per ADR 0040). (2) `rebar claim <id> --review`: instead of parsing precheck CommandErrors, the flag drives off the gate check directly at the claim.py:133 seam: when --review is set and the gate applies, call llm.claim_gate_check(ticket_id); if it reports not-ok, run review_plan(sign=True), then proceed into the normal plan_review_precheck path (which re-checks and fails closed with the standard message if still stale). When the gate is disabled or the ticket type is exempt (plan_review_precheck would return None), --review prints a one-line notice \"plan-review gate not enabled for this ticket; --review skipped\" and the claim proceeds — never a silent no-op. The flag is NOT propagated through the parent-first cascade. (3) Help and docs: the real help sources are src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt and src/rebar/_cli/help/claim.txt; docs/cli-reference.md is generated by scripts/gen_cli_reference.py and is regenerated, not hand-edited. Both help texts state the flags are not atomic against concurrent store reconvergence and point at `review-plan --status`. Lock discipline: neither flag holds the store flock across the review — the edit/claim appends its own event under the normal short-lived lock, releases it, and only then invokes review_plan, which itself takes the lock only for the brief under-lock generation re-check at signing; the multi-minute LLM passes run with no lock held. Both flags are CLI-only (the MCP surface keeps its REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM fence). Alternative rejected: new fused verbs — no OSS precedent, larger surface.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer.py, src/rebar/_commands/claim.py, src/rebar/_cli/help/edit.txt, src/rebar/_cli/help/claim.txt, docs/cli-reference.md (regenerated via scripts/gen_cli_reference.py), tests/unit/test_review_flags.py (new).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a stubbed review_plan returning verdict dicts: bare `--review` parses without consuming a following token (an edit with `--review --priority 1` keeps both); edit --review runs review after the EDIT commit and maps PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE stubs to exits 0/1/2; a BLOCK leaves the edit committed; claim --review triggers a review only when claim_gate_check reports not-ok, prints the gate-disabled notice for a bug-type ticket and claims anyway, and fails closed when the post-review recheck still fails; the parent cascade never receives the flag; a review stub that itself acquires the store flock succeeds under both flags.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bare --review parses as a valueless flag without swallowing the next token (checked: parser unit test).\n- [ ] edit --review runs the review strictly after the EDIT commit and exits with _disposition_exit_code(result, indeterminate_code=2) (checked: unit test recording call order and exit codes for PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE stubs).\n- [ ] claim --review reviews only when claim_gate_check reports not-ok, prints the skip notice when the gate does not apply, and never propagates through the parent cascade (checked: unit tests).\n- [ ] Help sources document non-atomicity and reference review-plan --status, and docs/cli-reference.md is regenerated (checked: help-text assertions; regenerated file committed).\n- [ ] The store lock is not held while the review runs: a review stub that acquires the store flock succeeds under both flags (checked: unit test)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785390736182534001,"uuid":"07f3ae9d-902a-4c28-9b3d-09532f0db9da"}